  "interpretation": [
    "v2 public replay review passed without a truth-rank board:1,024 prefixes,2,560 own random choices,392 retained captured-disclosure occurrences. Its much larger increment was specific to controlled random-own-policy contexts.",
    "Under actual frozen native choices, heldout mixed-cohort Flag log-score gain is only0.0342,0.0428,0.0149,0.0099bits after decisions1\u20134. Exact-prefix support declines84/160 to37/160, and only21,20,6,6 predictions change.",
    "The hard model already achieves100%top Flag accuracy on the template subset by enemy decision3 in this bounded sample; little headroom remains there.",
    "On exact procedural armies, first-step lookup gain is negative(\u22120.0528bits); one changed prediction lowers trueFlag probability0.2433->0.0754. Three of32 procedural forecasts are98.5\u201399.0%confidently wrong under both baseline and lookup. All32 become background-only by decision2.",
    "Do not sum per-step gains. They measure complete correlated prefixes, and neither entropy reduction nor these prediction scores demonstrate improved moves.",
    "Keeping the misspecified uniform background unchanged isolates lookup behavior, but does not solve its early confident errors. Source-faithful procedural background research is a more consequential next hypothesis."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only four fixed own formations, eight known source templates,32 procedural armies and one side/turn context.",
